{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into a perception plant (sensing obstacles) and a motion plant (executing motion commands). The specification binds perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration. All uncontrollable events are total in every state, and every non-terminal state enables exactly one controllable. Recovery states are one-shot and only reached by obstacle events. Forward/random_walk is prioritized in clear states; rotate/move_backward is used only for recovery. Full_rotate is reserved for repeated or dead-end recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and motion into distinct plants for modularity and clarity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-maximizing policy: forward/random_walk in clear, rotate/move_backward in obstacle states, and full_rotate only as last resort."
